<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<assemblage xml:id="boltzmann-transitions">
    <title>Before and After Boltzmann: From Mysterious Variable to Profound Understanding </title>
    <p>
      Before Boltzmann and his formulation of entropy <fn><xref ref="def-boltzmann-entropy"/></fn>, <alert>entropy</alert> was an esoteric-like thermodynamic quantity <m>S</m>.
      Boltzmann was able to frame this headache of a physical quantity as a combinatorial statement rooted in basic counting and leveraged the fact logarithms have the property
      that
      <md>
        \log{\Omega_A \times \Omega_B} = \log\Omega_A + \log\Omega_B
      </md>
    </p>
 </assemblage>